# Normalize line endings in the repository AND in the working tree on every
# platform. Without `eol=lf`, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true gets a
# CRLF working tree, which fails Prettier's endOfLine rule and produces diffs
# that are invisible on one platform and total on the other.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shims have to keep CRLF to remain executable.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4  binary
*.zip  binary

# Generated: collapsed by default in review and excluded from language stats.
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`. That marks a file binary and hides its diff outright,
# which is exactly backwards for these two: the lockfile diff is how an unexpected
# transitive dependency gets spotted, and openapi.json is the API contract the
# frontend is checked against. Both must stay readable when expanded.
pnpm-lock.yaml        linguist-generated=true
apps/api/openapi.json linguist-generated=true
